(ns aiueos.uefi-boot-fixture)

;; The kernel the loader's boot stage JUMPS to -- the smallest amu-produced
;; kernel image whose entry answers on the debug console and then takes the
;; machine away from QEMU with its own exit code.
;;
;; Why this exists (JUN-31): the fs-stage fixture (`examples/i64-semantics.kotoba`
;; in amu) is a program whose `main` returns 0. A loader that jumped to it would
;; execute `ret` with no return address and triple-fault -- a failure that is
;; indistinguishable from a loader that never jumped at all. Boot needs a kernel
;; that ANSWERS: `B` on the debug console (port 0xE9, the same channel the
;; loader's marks use) and `out 0xf4, 21`, which makes QEMU stop with
;; (21 << 1) | 1 = 43. The loader's own fallback exit is 33 (16 << 1 | 1), so
;; 43 on the QEMU status line can only come from a kernel that ran.
;;
;; The two port writes are the contract's `:boot` evidence operations
;; (`contracts/value-runtime-kernel-image-v1.edn`: kernel-out-u8, kernel-out-u32),
;; spelled here with their raw port numbers: 233 = 0xE9 debugcon, 244 = 0xF4
;; isa-debug-exit.

(defn main []
  (kernel-out-u8 233 66)
  (kernel-out-u32 244 21))
